# Git Rules

## Scope

A task should produce a coherent set of changes.

Avoid mixing:

- feature implementation;
- unrelated refactoring;
- formatting;
- dependency upgrades.

## Commit

When commits are requested, prefer semantic commits:

feat(...)
fix(...)
test(...)
refactor(...)
docs(...)
chore(...)

## Do not

Do not:

- rewrite unrelated history;
- reset user work;
- delete changes you did not create;
- modify unrelated files without reason.

## User changes

Treat existing uncommitted user changes as protected.

Do not overwrite them.

Before making destructive changes, stop and report.